From 0822301635a5699c9d9dcf474bc2b829aeedbd89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:01:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NodalBlockJacobi: block size checked on all processes, empty
 processes tested
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The size of the blocks of an operator applied without assembly is
checked against the number of components of the unknowns, stored in the
settings at the generation, before the computation of the blocks, which
is collective: the check failed only on the processes owning unknowns,
the other ones being then blocked in the Krylov solver. The right hand
side of the LU solves of the native backend of MFEM is made valid where
MFEM computes (NativeBatchedLinAlg::LUSolve gets it by Write).

The test checks a process owning no element, and an operator giving its
nodal blocks as the tangent operator applied without assembly does: same
preconditioner as with its matrix, blocks of size one refused on all the
processes. The Lamé coefficients of the elasticity system of the tests
are members, the bilinear form keeping pointers to them, and its types
are documented.

Docs: blocks of size one are refused for an operator applied without
assembly; the damping changes the stopping test of the Krylov solvers
with an absolute tolerance.
